  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">NCC QUEBEC</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project is composed of securement activities that will occur on private lands at three locations in Coastal/maritime Qubec (Mingan..Archipelago, Magdalen Islands and Longue-Rive). Activities will occur near Nature Reserves, designated Wildlife Refuges or National Parks,..and target habitat requirements of migratory bird species affected by the BP oil spill. Specifically, this project will protect 279 acres..(182 wetland, 97 upland acres) of important North Atlantic coastal habitats in Eastern Quebec from drainage, conversion, development, and other..critical threats. Habitats protected under this proposal will protect in perpetuity staging and/or breeding habitat for at least 5 species..impacted by the BP oil spill across four sites, directly linked to the populations of affected species targeted in the proposal that migrate..through or have wintering locations in the Gulf of Mexico region.</narrative>
  </description>
